Upstream prototypes (Week 11) - detailed usage
==============================================

1) What is included
-------------------
- los_forecast.py
  Core rule-based LOS forecast engine with confidence scoring.

- daily_huddle_board.py
  Reads sample_patients.csv and generates:
  out/daily_huddle_board.html
  (priority-sorted board for daily bed/discharge huddle).

- communication_flow.py
  Reads sample_patients.csv and generates:
  out/patient_message_schedule.csv
  (D-2 / D-1 / D0 communication schedule).

- sample_patients.csv
  Broad synthetic dataset (multiple procedures and care constraints).

- github-io/index.html
  Front-end demo page (interactive LOS calculator + communication preview).

- publish_github_pages.sh
  One-command script to regenerate artifacts, commit, push, and publish via GitHub Pages.


2) Local quick start (Linux)
----------------------------
cd 6.Experiments/upstream-prototypes
python3 --version
python3 daily_huddle_board.py
python3 communication_flow.py

Open:
- out/daily_huddle_board.html in a browser
- out/patient_message_schedule.csv in spreadsheet editor


3) Expected outputs
-------------------
After running scripts, you should have:
- out/daily_huddle_board.html
  Columns: ID, patient, procedure, predicted LOS, expected discharge date,
  confidence label/score, early coordination flag, blockers, priority score.

- out/patient_message_schedule.csv
  Rows per patient for D-2, D-1, D0 with message text template.


4) How to adjust for your team meeting demo
-------------------------------------------
- Edit sample_patients.csv
  Add/remove rows or blockers to simulate realistic Saint-Luc scenarios.

- Re-run:
  python3 daily_huddle_board.py
  python3 communication_flow.py

- Present:
  1) LOS prediction logic (engine),
  2) operational board (huddle support),
  3) patient communication timeline.


5) Publish on GitHub Pages (automated, iterative)
--------------------------------------------------
Use the script for first publish and all updates:

cd 6.Experiments/upstream-prototypes
chmod +x publish_github_pages.sh
./publish_github_pages.sh Lord-Melflam saint-luc-bouges-g6-upstream-prototypes /

What the script does:
1. Creates/uses .venv
2. Regenerates out/ artifacts
3. Initializes git repo if needed
4. Creates or connects to GitHub repo
5. Commits changes
6. Pushes main branch
7. Enables GitHub Pages if not already enabled

Default URL:
https://lord-melflam.github.io/saint-luc-bouges-g6-upstream-prototypes/

For subsequent updates:
./publish_github_pages.sh

Optional custom commit message:
./publish_github_pages.sh Lord-Melflam saint-luc-bouges-g6-upstream-prototypes / "Tune LOS weighting"


6) Notes for portfolio/slides
-----------------------------
You can claim a functional prototype chain:
- Forecast (predict and confidence),
- Coordination (daily board),
- Communication (scheduled messages).

This is enough for a credible technical proof-of-concept even without hospital system integration.


7) What to do with the Python code (short answer)
-------------------------------------------------
Keep the Python code as your reproducible backend prototype (forecast + board + communication schedule), and use the web page as the presentation layer.
Workflow: edit CSV -> run Python scripts -> publish via script.
